  "body": "**Stacked on #476** (#339 slice 1, fixture mesh). Slice 5 of #339 per the triage on the issue: link and retract routing around fixtures.\n\n## What changed\nNew `crates/app/src/operation/fixture_route.rs`, with one hook in `generate.rs` before the verify pass. It runs for upright mill paths only.\n\n**The rule:**\n- **What a link is:** the longest run of straight rapids between two non-rapid moves, or a path end.\n- **When it counts as struck:** the gate's own fixture laws flag it. That's #464's whole-stack law (d2) plus #476's mesh acquittal, so a routed link is judged exactly as the post gate will judge it.\n- **The fix:** a struck link becomes three G0 moves: up at its start XY, across, down to its end. The height is the higher of the link's own top and the highest box top under the traverse plus 5 mm (`ROUTE_GAP`). \"Under the traverse\" means every box the widest band reaches along the XY segment.\n- **The cap:** the machine's stated Z stroke (WCS origin Z plus the top of the stroke), keeping at least 0.5 mm over the steel. Steel taller than that **refuses generation by name**: \"the link at moves i..j … cannot clear fixture 'Clamp1': its steel stands to Z …, and the machine's Z stroke tops out at Z …\". With no stroke stated there is no cap, as everywhere else.\n- **Re-judging:** the re-laid link is judged again. If it's still struck, the steel stands over the link's own end column and no height helps. The link is then left as laid, its `FixtureHit` still blocks the post by name, and a path note says why.\n- **Notes:** every raised link gets a path note: how many rose, from where, over which fixture, to what Z.\n\n**Left as today (report-only):**\n- **Keep-down feed links.** In the CL stream they look exactly like cuts, so lifting one could silently skip a cut. They're only taken inside the cut area, so if one hits steel the cuts beside it hit too, and the post is refused anyway. A keep-down **rapid** run at depth does become retract, traverse and plunge.\n- **Other paths:** posed and rotary paths, lathe tools, paths with canned cycles (a traverse inserted between holes could post as a drill), thread or probe records, and runs inside a compensated span.\n\n**Posted G-code changes only** for documents with a link the fixture laws strike, and only those links' G0 moves. Documents without fixtures return early untouched, and links that already clear are never rewritten, so all goldens are unchanged.\n\n`docs/decisions/339-fixture-routing.md`\n\n## How tested\n- **New app `fixture_route`** (6 tests):\n  - A Contour around two blocks with a strap clamp to Z 40 between them, at clearance 25. As generated, the gate refuses (\"strikes a fixture\"). After the fix, the links rise to Z 45, the post is clean, the cuts are identical, and the note names Clamp1.\n  - A clamp the links already clear leaves the path byte for byte.\n  - A 100 mm Z stroke still routes over the 40 mm clamp, while a 400 mm clamp refuses generation naming 'Clamp1' and \"Z 400.000\".\n  - A stay-down rapid link becomes retract, traverse and plunge. Clear steel and no steel are untouched.\n  - Steel over a link's own end is left as laid and said.\n  - A ceiling under the steel refuses, and a ceiling over it caps the rise.\n- **Existing suites keep their verdicts:** fixtures (14), fixture_mesh (3), fixture_law_gaps (3), posting (17), tool_body (8). All app test binaries passed in the quick gate.\n- `clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (draft)\nThis changes posted G-code (raised G0 links) for documents with struck fixtures, so it's a draft until a Hub or machine run. It needs a project with a clamp between features.\n\nChangelog: Links and retracts that would strike a fixture are raised over the steel (a clamp taller than the machine's Z stroke refuses generation by name) instead of only being reported (#339)\n\nRefs #339\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
